Original copyright and license headers are retained in each derived file.

Local changes introduce a cumulative decoder allocation budget before allocating
Huffman groups/nodes/codes, color caches, image/transform/meta-image buffers,
alpha planes and VP8 partition/frame storage. The WebP adapter no longer
registers an unrestricted global image decoder. It checks alpha/frame size
agreement. VP8 and RIFF implementations remain the pinned x/image dependency.
The VP8 reservation formula must be re-audited when that dependency is upgraded.

The testdata/*.webp images are original synthetic patterns created for Misa,
encoded once using Pillow/libwebp. They contain no third-party image assets.
No encoder is needed for builds or tests. Lossless rgba pixels are:
  R=x*16, G=y*16, B=(x+y)*8, A=32+(x+y)*7, for 0<=x,y<16.
RGB/RGBA lossy fixtures encode the same pattern. Palette fixtures cycle n colors
for n=2,4,16,256 with R=i*255/(n-1), G=(i*97)%256, B=(i*53)%256.
